WEBVTT

00:04.504 --> 00:08.425
You're so lucky.
I wish I was on the white team, too.

00:08.508 --> 00:10.552
White is the color of my Sakamoto!

00:10.635 --> 00:12.095
Creepy otaku.

00:19.394 --> 00:21.730
This was hand-made!

00:22.856 --> 00:24.691
My Sakamoto!

00:24.774 --> 00:28.903
I think people like you
who are obsessed about someone

00:29.446 --> 00:33.241
are avoiding facing your own reality
'cause you don't have a life.

00:35.368 --> 00:36.536
What's that for?

00:37.037 --> 00:38.288
You got on my nerves.

00:38.955 --> 00:39.789
So, what?

00:40.874 --> 00:43.918
You're criticizing how I live my life?

00:46.838 --> 00:50.925
If you mock my devotion for Sakamoto,
you deserve to die.

00:52.427 --> 00:53.261
<i>Yikes!</i>

00:58.224 --> 00:59.476
Now, then.

01:00.477 --> 01:03.104
Gaku, you'd better get ready, too.

01:03.688 --> 01:04.564
'Kay.

01:05.106 --> 01:07.984
Is this even gonna be fun, though?

01:08.485 --> 01:12.030
It's not supposed to be. This is work.

02:44.706 --> 02:45.540
<i>That's right...</i>

02:45.623 --> 02:46.457
MUTUAL FANS

02:46.541 --> 02:47.709
<i>I have to do it.</i>

02:48.334 --> 02:50.169
<i>Otherwise, these people will die.</i>

02:51.963 --> 02:53.464
<i>Pull yourself together, Akira!</i>

02:54.424 --> 02:55.508
<i>Open your eyes.</i>

02:57.218 --> 02:59.053
<i>If the alternative is losing someone,</i>

03:01.431 --> 03:02.307
<i>then I...</i>

03:08.730 --> 03:09.981
<i>I'd rather be an assassin.</i>

03:22.577 --> 03:24.662
Calm down, Akira.

03:27.248 --> 03:28.166
Akira,

03:29.083 --> 03:31.169
what's your family name?

03:33.504 --> 03:34.380
It's Akao...

03:35.423 --> 03:38.051
My name is Akira Akao.

03:42.263 --> 03:44.057
JCC SHOOTING RANGE

03:48.353 --> 03:52.440
Shooting a gun is kinda like
driving a car, y'know?

03:53.191 --> 03:55.902
You can tell a lot about someone
just by their grip.

03:56.611 --> 03:57.445
So lemme guess.

03:58.613 --> 03:59.530
You guys

03:59.614 --> 04:03.826
are the ones slowing down traffic
in highway merge lanes, aren't ya?

04:04.369 --> 04:05.620
Lousy shooters.

04:06.829 --> 04:07.747
This is stupid.

04:08.248 --> 04:11.334
Can you believe she's proud
about shooting a still target?

04:11.417 --> 04:14.170
You'd never use that many bullets
in real combat, anyway.

04:14.254 --> 04:17.131
<i>You guys</i> are the ones who challenged <i>me!</i>

04:17.215 --> 04:19.801
You'd better keep your word
and buy me lunch!

04:19.884 --> 04:21.010
Or I'll kill you!

04:26.182 --> 04:27.308
<i>Mr. Taro?</i>

04:29.310 --> 04:30.561
Is everything okay?

04:31.688 --> 04:32.563
Akira,

04:33.356 --> 04:36.067
are you related to Rion Akao?

04:37.610 --> 04:40.780
Do you know something about Rion?

04:40.863 --> 04:43.616
I'm Rion's niece.

04:44.867 --> 04:47.787
I came here hoping I could find her.

05:05.430 --> 05:08.766
Come on, boys! Let's see what you've got!

05:11.102 --> 05:13.980
Come on. Let's kill her together, Shin.

05:14.063 --> 05:16.941
I didn't come here to have a kill-off!

05:17.025 --> 05:19.402
Hey. You came in
the same group as her, right?

05:19.485 --> 05:20.778
Could you go stop her?

05:21.362 --> 05:22.572
Um, more importantly,

05:23.239 --> 05:24.115
we're approaching a--

05:24.198 --> 05:27.618
Come on, Shin, let's kill her together.

05:27.702 --> 05:29.203
I told you I'm not gonna kill!

05:29.704 --> 05:31.539
Why don't you just do it yourself?

05:31.622 --> 05:33.374
They said to work as a team.

05:33.458 --> 05:35.501
Hey, I think we should stop before--

05:35.585 --> 05:39.422
What happened to that whole
lone-wolf act from the airplane?

05:43.009 --> 05:45.261
She's shooting at... us!

05:51.476 --> 05:52.435
Oh.

06:03.196 --> 06:04.030
So cold...

06:06.157 --> 06:07.325
Thanks for saving us,

06:07.825 --> 06:09.035
uh...

06:10.536 --> 06:11.704
Kaji.

06:12.872 --> 06:14.540
I don't feel very good...

06:15.124 --> 06:19.253
Why's that girl so crazy about
Mr. Sakamoto, anyway?

06:19.337 --> 06:20.338
Who knows.

06:21.798 --> 06:22.882
I feel nauseous.

06:23.424 --> 06:25.259
Ooh, what'd you say?

06:25.343 --> 06:27.261
You wanna know why?

06:27.345 --> 06:29.013
What are you, a monkey?

06:29.597 --> 06:30.807
You see,

06:31.724 --> 06:33.893
Sakamoto is like a God to me.

06:35.686 --> 06:40.066
<i>The first time I laid eyes on Sakamoto,
I thought my heart might stop beating.</i>

06:43.277 --> 06:46.572
<i>You fought so elegantly,
showing no emotion...</i>

06:47.156 --> 06:49.575
<i>Compared to me,
stuck in my stupid worries,</i>

06:49.659 --> 06:51.994
<i>it was like you were a different species.</i>

06:53.454 --> 06:55.248
<i>I searched for a song that suits him.</i>

06:55.873 --> 06:57.500
<i>I started enjoying music.</i>

06:58.501 --> 07:03.214
<i>I dyed my hair and started to wear makeup
so I'd feel proud to call myself his fan.</i>

07:03.840 --> 07:05.675
<i>I started enjoying getting dressed up.</i>

07:07.426 --> 07:10.805
<i>I practiced my conversational skills
in case I met him one day.</i>

07:11.389 --> 07:12.932
<i>I started making friends.</i>

07:13.891 --> 07:17.854
<i>Thanks to Sakamoto,
my whole world became brighter.</i>

07:22.984 --> 07:23.818
That's why...

07:25.069 --> 07:27.905
there's no way in hell
I'd let anyone criticize it.

07:30.867 --> 07:32.243
Damn it!

07:32.326 --> 07:33.953
Mafuyu! You ready to fight?

07:34.036 --> 07:36.122
Nah... I feel nauseous.

07:36.205 --> 07:38.082
You've gotta be kidding me!

07:38.791 --> 07:40.209
I guess I have no choice...

07:41.627 --> 07:42.628
Bring it on.

07:42.712 --> 07:43.629
I'll take you down.

07:44.172 --> 07:46.007
Wait a minute!

07:46.090 --> 07:48.885
That pose,
the way you cracked your shoulder,

07:48.968 --> 07:51.554
that's like, totally
Sakamoto's pre-combat routine!

07:53.514 --> 07:55.850
You couldn't mimic
such niche details, unless...

07:55.933 --> 07:58.102
Are you a Sakamoto fan?

07:59.228 --> 08:01.147
Shin, you're an otaku, too?

08:01.230 --> 08:02.940
<i>Shit! She caught me...</i>

08:03.441 --> 08:06.319
No way! This is so awesome!

08:06.402 --> 08:09.322
I've never met someone
who could keep up with me!

08:09.405 --> 08:12.408
Tell me, what's your
favorite thing about Sakamoto?

08:12.492 --> 08:13.701
My favorite thing is

08:13.784 --> 08:16.787
his cool attitude,
as if he has no emotion!

08:17.622 --> 08:21.459
He's like a real-life murder machine,
like, talk about slay!

08:22.168 --> 08:23.002
You're wrong.

08:24.837 --> 08:26.380
I know why you'd think that.

08:27.715 --> 08:29.634
I used to feel the same way.

08:30.551 --> 08:31.385
But, no.

08:31.469 --> 08:32.845
Now, Mr. Sakamoto endures

08:34.472 --> 08:35.973
<i>no matter how bad business is,</i>

08:36.474 --> 08:38.559
<i>and he'd never fire us
even to stay afloat.</i>

08:39.227 --> 08:41.562
<i>He's a warm-hearted person.</i>

08:43.064 --> 08:44.273
What are you talking about?

08:44.357 --> 08:45.399
So, what happens

08:45.483 --> 08:48.361
if people keep saying
"He's the invincible hit man!"

08:48.444 --> 08:50.363
and keeps him at arm's length?

08:51.072 --> 08:53.199
Who can Mr. Sakamoto lean on?

08:54.909 --> 08:58.037
I'm not going to use my admiration
as an excuse anymore.

09:00.164 --> 09:02.250
I'm going to become as good as him.

09:03.834 --> 09:06.462
I'm going to become his partner,
not a sidekick.

09:10.341 --> 09:11.634
How dare you.

09:11.717 --> 09:13.678
The way you've been blabbing on...

09:14.262 --> 09:17.890
Do you think you understand
Sakamoto better than I do?

09:18.516 --> 09:21.852
Do you think you're the number one fan?
That you could one-up me?

09:22.520 --> 09:24.939
Yeah, right. No way.

09:25.022 --> 09:27.942
Shut up, shut up, shut up, shut up!

09:28.025 --> 09:29.986
I've never felt so irritated.

09:31.445 --> 09:32.780
Of course...

09:32.863 --> 09:34.490
This feeling is what they call

09:36.492 --> 09:37.451
"refusal to share."

09:37.535 --> 09:38.452
REFUSAL TO SHARE

09:41.163 --> 09:44.333
<i>Once again, you've blessed me
with a whole new emotion.</i>

09:44.417 --> 09:46.419
<i>Thank you, Sakamoto.</i>

09:48.546 --> 09:49.797
Get out of the picture.

09:50.590 --> 09:52.842
Sakamoto working with a partner?

09:58.306 --> 10:00.516
That's not part of the lore!

10:06.105 --> 10:08.316
That Toramaru kid is insane.

10:09.108 --> 10:10.901
No wonder she's got recommendations.

10:11.569 --> 10:15.031
Speaking of which,
you're really good too, Shinaya.

10:15.615 --> 10:17.450
We already have three tails.

10:17.533 --> 10:19.118
Keep up the good work for us.

10:21.370 --> 10:22.496
What? Do you sense an enemy?

10:31.839 --> 10:33.507
You idiot, what are you doing?!

10:33.591 --> 10:37.219
You'll get disqualified!
Put that back on, hurry!

10:38.596 --> 10:39.680
Shinaya?

11:01.494 --> 11:02.787
Impressive!

11:02.870 --> 11:05.164
I can't get you at all!

11:05.247 --> 11:07.291
It feels like you're reading my mind.

11:07.875 --> 11:10.378
I'm starting to think
you're legit psychic.

11:11.003 --> 11:14.256
Still, all you do is
dodge my attacks, y'know?

11:18.135 --> 11:20.054
You don't deserve to be a Sakamoto fan.

11:22.223 --> 11:25.476
<i>That weapon she's got
is a pain in the neck.</i>

11:26.519 --> 11:27.937
Shin...

11:28.020 --> 11:30.564
Should I go help him?

11:31.107 --> 11:33.150
But I still feel really sick...

11:34.068 --> 11:35.277
<i>Perhaps...</i>

11:35.820 --> 11:37.655
<i>I should go and help him out?</i>

11:38.280 --> 11:39.240
<i>But,</i>

11:39.323 --> 11:40.908
<i>what do I say?</i>

11:41.534 --> 11:44.912
<i>"Hey man, I've got your back"? But, like...</i>

11:44.995 --> 11:47.123
<i>I don't want them to think I was being</i>

11:47.206 --> 11:48.541
<i>too friendly too soon.</i>

11:49.291 --> 11:51.168
<i>Should I join without saying anything?</i>

11:51.919 --> 11:53.170
<i>Would it be more natural?</i>

11:55.923 --> 11:56.757
<i>I know.</i>

11:57.299 --> 11:59.635
<i>I'll wait until they say something to me.</i>

12:01.137 --> 12:04.390
<i>Kaji is extremely shy around new people.</i>

12:05.057 --> 12:06.183
<i>For now,</i>

12:06.267 --> 12:08.352
<i>I'll start by rubbing his back.</i>

12:08.978 --> 12:10.604
Hey, don't touch me.

12:28.497 --> 12:30.374
You like counter-attacks?

12:32.084 --> 12:35.880
If that's your thing,
you gotta get me in a single blow.

12:40.885 --> 12:42.845
<i>Man, she has stamina.</i>

12:43.596 --> 12:45.514
<i>What am I gonna do?</i>

12:45.598 --> 12:47.099
<i>What would Mr. Sakamoto--</i>

12:48.434 --> 12:49.560
<i>No!</i>

12:49.643 --> 12:51.270
<i>I gotta stop thinking like that.</i>

12:51.812 --> 12:54.857
<i>I'm not his size
and I don't have his strength.</i>

12:55.608 --> 12:57.735
<i>I have to find my way of winning this.</i>

12:57.818 --> 12:58.777
<i>Figure it out.</i>

12:59.320 --> 13:01.864
<i>What can I do in this situation?</i>

13:16.337 --> 13:19.089
You will never be in Sakamoto's league.

13:24.470 --> 13:25.429
Ouch!

13:25.971 --> 13:28.974
I told you, all these light hits...

13:31.727 --> 13:33.103
won't make a--

13:40.694 --> 13:42.571
Did you know waterfalls can trap fish?

13:43.864 --> 13:45.699
I could hear all the fish's thoughts.

13:48.118 --> 13:52.039
Taking advantage of the terrain is
something I learned from Mr. Sakamoto.

13:55.918 --> 13:58.087
<i>You gotta get me in a single blow.</i>

13:59.547 --> 14:00.756
Killer instinct,

14:01.590 --> 14:02.424
huh...

14:03.259 --> 14:04.927
Guess I should go join Mafuyu.

14:06.136 --> 14:09.223
<i>No, Sakamoto!</i>

14:10.808 --> 14:11.725
What the?

14:12.518 --> 14:13.352
<i>Can't... breathe...</i>

14:16.021 --> 14:16.981
Damn it!

14:29.910 --> 14:30.828
<i>There she is.</i>

14:32.162 --> 14:34.540
<i>Her mini Sakamoto got stuck?</i>

14:34.623 --> 14:35.833
<i>Jeez.</i>

14:35.916 --> 14:37.251
<i>She's hardcore for sure.</i>

14:56.061 --> 14:57.021
Sakamoto!

14:59.940 --> 15:01.233
You're alright!

15:02.067 --> 15:03.611
I won't save you next time.

15:04.361 --> 15:05.237
You?

15:05.738 --> 15:07.698
Why did you save my life?

15:11.035 --> 15:14.872
I told you I could understand
why you admire Mr. Sakamoto.

15:15.581 --> 15:16.582
Besides...

15:18.083 --> 15:20.252
he wouldn't have left you to drown.

15:20.920 --> 15:22.004
That's why.

15:29.345 --> 15:30.262
It's all yours...

15:31.764 --> 15:35.601
I'm saying you can have the title
of number one fan!

15:35.684 --> 15:37.102
Keep me out of it!

15:37.186 --> 15:40.105
Why?! We can grow the community together!

15:40.189 --> 15:41.565
- Let's talk more!
- What a pain...

15:42.191 --> 15:43.317
- Oh, I know,
- Please!

15:43.400 --> 15:45.986
why don't you gimme your tail
instead of that doll.

16:03.545 --> 16:05.881
Shoot, it's lagging a bit.

16:05.965 --> 16:09.385
Guess I'll just pretend it's an FPS game.

16:10.219 --> 16:11.720
<i>Alright then...</i>

16:13.263 --> 16:14.932
<i>Time to hunt for new members.</i>

16:33.701 --> 16:34.994
Shin!

16:35.077 --> 16:36.203
Mafuyu, Kaji.

16:36.829 --> 16:38.163
What's up with him?

16:38.706 --> 16:40.791
He's the other one with recommendations.

16:50.884 --> 16:53.178
I think I've seen this guy before.

16:54.013 --> 16:55.305
Where do I know him from?

16:57.224 --> 17:01.228
Gaku, stop fooling around
and start recruiting.

17:01.311 --> 17:03.814
It's not like any of 'em will be any good.

17:03.897 --> 17:05.774
Now, now. Don't give up.

17:06.442 --> 17:07.568
Boss.

17:08.235 --> 17:10.696
An organization is made up of individuals.

17:11.572 --> 17:13.907
I am impressed by this thing.

17:14.700 --> 17:15.993
Virtual reality, was it?

17:16.618 --> 17:19.163
Who knew hit men could work remotely.

17:20.956 --> 17:22.833
Mr. Kashima, I think it's broken.

17:23.792 --> 17:25.210
I can't move it at all.

17:25.294 --> 17:27.629
Put your goggles on.

17:27.713 --> 17:28.797
Um,

17:28.881 --> 17:30.382
could you do it for me?

17:30.466 --> 17:32.009
Honestly...

17:35.179 --> 17:40.017
Candidate number 208, uh...
What was your name again?

17:40.100 --> 17:41.101
Shinaya.

17:41.685 --> 17:42.603
Right, Mr. Shinaya.

17:43.187 --> 17:45.397
You're disqualified
for breaking the rules.

17:45.481 --> 17:48.275
What? Which rule did he break?

17:48.942 --> 17:51.612
And why'd he get caught so easily?

17:51.695 --> 17:55.365
We've told you that you'd be considered
dead if you didn't have a tail on.

17:55.991 --> 17:57.326
No zombies, please.

17:59.870 --> 18:00.704
It's in my way.

18:02.122 --> 18:03.373
On our way here,

18:03.999 --> 18:06.460
<i>we passed four bodies of candidates.</i>

18:07.211 --> 18:09.963
Are you responsible for them too, Shinaya?

18:14.426 --> 18:17.638
Do you know what
you must have as a hit man?

18:18.222 --> 18:19.181
Love

18:19.765 --> 18:20.682
and discipline.

18:21.266 --> 18:25.145
We don't need thrill killers at the JCC.

18:25.229 --> 18:27.689
You gotta respect how we operate as pros.

18:27.773 --> 18:31.652
We make a living out of this, you know?

18:34.279 --> 18:35.280
What's wrong?

18:35.823 --> 18:36.657
Nothing.

18:37.658 --> 18:40.619
You know, I hate teachers.

18:42.246 --> 18:44.039
So. We won't kill you,

18:44.123 --> 18:47.126
but you'll have to sit it out
until the exam is--

18:49.503 --> 18:50.671
Found a weapon.

18:57.761 --> 18:58.762
Fire.

19:06.520 --> 19:07.855
He's not bad.

19:11.775 --> 19:13.944
I told you to show some respect!

19:31.670 --> 19:33.338
He's out of his mind.

19:36.049 --> 19:38.093
Suppose the exam will have to wait.

19:39.052 --> 19:40.804
You three, run while you can.

19:41.430 --> 19:43.390
You young people
have a future ahead of you.

19:48.395 --> 19:50.731
Hurry up, Shin. Let's go!

19:52.024 --> 19:53.233
You go ahead.

19:55.569 --> 19:57.529
If I can't fight what I'm facing now,

19:57.613 --> 20:00.073
I can't see a future where I'm stronger!

20:04.077 --> 20:06.997
You're gonna die young, kid.

20:14.755 --> 20:15.714
<i>Oh no...</i>

20:16.256 --> 20:17.216
<i>That fight earlier...</i>

20:18.008 --> 20:19.009
<i>used up my time...</i>

20:27.935 --> 20:29.061
What on earth?

20:35.192 --> 20:37.152
Trying to outshine us? No fair.

20:37.653 --> 20:39.613
I know, right?

20:40.906 --> 20:42.032
You two...

20:44.409 --> 20:46.620
Alright, nice.

20:47.412 --> 20:50.290
We've got some challengers.

22:23.967 --> 22:27.179
I wonder how the exam's going
for Mr. Manager and Shin.

22:27.763 --> 22:29.973
It must be a breeze for them!

22:31.224 --> 22:32.851
I'm a little worried.

22:33.393 --> 22:35.729
I wonder if they're getting proper food...

22:36.605 --> 22:38.690
Taro will easily opt for instant noodles.

22:39.316 --> 22:42.986
Who knows? Maybe they're eating
snakes and grasshoppers.

22:43.737 --> 22:45.238
That's not funny!

22:47.491 --> 22:50.327
Mr. Taro, we gathered
the edible wild greens you wanted.

22:50.410 --> 22:51.953
A whole heap of 'em!

22:52.496 --> 22:53.914
Thanks, guys.

23:15.894 --> 23:17.979
This is delicious.

23:18.063 --> 23:20.023
Packed with nutrition, too.

23:22.067 --> 23:24.820
Somehow, I enjoy cooking
when I'm camping out.

23:24.903 --> 23:25.904
Subtitle translation by: Yuka Kristi
